Ambarīṣa halts at Puṣkara with Śunaḥśēpa --- Śunaḥśēpa falls at Viśvāmitra's lap begging rescue --- Viśvāmitra asks sons to become the sacrificial victim --- Sons scornfully refuse the exchange --- Viśvāmitra curses sons to eat dog meat for thousand years --- Viśvāmitra gives Śunaḥśēpa two saving hymns --- Ambarīṣa binds Śunaḥśēpa to Viṣṇu post --- Śunaḥśēpa praises Indra and Upēndra --- Indra grants Śunaḥśēpa long life --- Ambarīṣa completes sacrifice while Viśvāmitra resumes austerities